Fixes checkbox and radio button width in Twenty Nineteen and Twenty Seventeen themes.

The CSS rule `.single-product form.cart input{width:5em}` was setting the width for ALL input types, making checkboxes and radio buttons wider than they are tall.

Changes:
- Updated CSS selector from `input` to `input[type="number"]` in twenty-nineteen.scss
- Updated CSS selector from `input` to `input[type="number"]` in twenty-seventeen.scss
- This ensures only quantity input fields receive the width styling

Fixes #29264.
